so the typical way to get an artifact weapon is by sacrificing to your god-
if you do that enough, your god will give you an artifact-- for more
details, see the artifact spoilers for which ones can be given as gifts..
if you are lawful, you can get Excalibur by #dipping a long sword
into a fountain.  Sometimes, you can just find artifacts laying around, but
that is pretty rare.

As far as armor- the gnomish mines tend to be a good place to pick up mithril,
which is very good armor until you have a way to get dragon scale mail
[I would argue that dwarvish mithril is the best armor short of DSM,
 even though 2 types of plate mail provide 1 more point of AC, because (1)
 its lightweight and plate mail is heavy, (2) its provides MC of 3, while
 platemail only provides MC of 2, and (3) it wont rust or corrode,
 which platemail will (although crystal plate mail wont, but the first
 two points still hold for it)]

The other way to get good stuff, is of course a wish- for full details
(including suggested wishes), read the wishing spoiler.

